{#
  src/ioc-index-core.njk — the search index without its context quotes
  =====================================================================
  The same payload as /assets/data/ioc-index.json (see src/ioc-index.njk)
  minus the `contexts` table, which is 42% of the bytes and only matters once
  a reader searches for a phrase from a report. src/assets/js/ioc-search.js
  fetches this first and has a working search as soon as it lands, then
  fetches /assets/data/ioc-contexts.json in the background and re-runs the
  current query when the quotes arrive.

  To keep the file small, a record leaves out any key whose value is null,
  `[]` or 0, and an `r` of "remote-workers"; ioc-search.js reads a missing
  key as exactly that. See searchCore() in iocIndex.js.

  Source entries still carry their index into the contexts table, so the two
  files join by position. Both are built from one call, so they cannot drift.
  The full single-file index stays where it is for the no-script fallback and
  for anyone consuming it as data.
#}
